Origin: https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/0bb308eb4cf699e707efbcf97ffb70e46a176be7
Advisory: GHSA-vvx9-73fr-5jjx, CVE-2026-91769
Imported-by: backported to 7.2 by hand (zend_bool; tests use fixed port + phpt_notify/phpt_wait; CertificateGenerator.inc updated from PHP-8.2 for SAN support)

From 09a573fb97bf949b61cba54db39ba4cdedfb7db0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Zelenka <bukka@php.net>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 22:25:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-vvx9-73fr-5jjx: do not fall back to CN if the cert
 has a service ID

RFC 6125 6.4.4 forbids matching CN-ID if the certificate presents a DNS-ID,
SRV-ID or URI-ID. Falling back allowed a CA that validated only one of those
identities to leave an unvalidated CN to be matched as a host name.

IP-ID is left out as it is out of scope of RFC 6125 and suppressing CN there
would break IP-only SAN certificates.

Backport of php-src 0bb308eb4cf699e707efbcf97ffb70e46a176be7 (PHP-8.2) to PHP 7.2:
- zend_bool / 1 / 0 instead of bool / true / false
- tests: fixed port 64321 with phpt_notify()/phpt_wait() (7.2 ServerClientTestCase has no {{ ADDR }}), lowercase "unable to connect"
- tests: CertificateGenerator.inc updated to the PHP-8.2 version (subjectAltName support, explicit openssl.cnf for the CA so generated chains verify with OpenSSL 3), without the trailing comma in a call (PHP 7.3+)
